["entertainment/african-cinema-beyond-nollywood-explained","The Continent's Cinemas","African cinema beyond Nollywood is several industries with their own grammars: Senegal's essayistic tradition, South Africa's genre revival, Kenya's social realism and the streaming-era new wave. The map here is honest about coverage gaps.","The map","Regional industries with their own histories and forms.","Senegal's tradition","Essayistic cinema that treats film as argument.","South Africa's revival","Genre filmmaking with the country's politics attached.","East African realism","Kenya and Uganda's social-cinema grammar.","The streaming era","Distribution changed which African stories get financed.","Coverage honesty","What this desk has seen versus what it knows of.","African cinema is a continent of film traditions rather than a single industry. The map here keeps the coverage honest and the viewing list reachable.","home"],
["home/sink-drain-slow-unclog","The Four Rungs","The slow sink has four rungs: stopper, trap, branch and vent, cheapest first. Most bathroom sinks stall at the stopper and most kitchen sinks at the trap, and the plunger technique most people use is backwards.","The four rungs","Stopper, trap, branch, vent: the ladder's order.","The stopper","Hair and soap wrap the rod; ten minutes clears it.","The trap","Bucket and couplings: the classic contained mess.","Plunger technique","The wet-cloth and angle details that make plunging work.","Chemicals honestly","Why caustic drains are the last resort, not the first.","The vent line","Gurgling and slow-pull symptoms point to the stack.","A slow sink is a ladder with cheap rungs at the bottom. Start where the symptom points and the drain clears without a callout.","home"],
["home/fridge-door-not-sealing","The Seal Test And The Fix","A fridge door that will not seal is usually the gasket, sometimes the level and rarely the hinge: the dollar-bill test decides which, and the gasket fix is a warm-water job before it is a parts job.","The dollar-bill test","Close the bill in the door; the drag tells the story.","The gasket","Warm water and silicone grease restore most seals.","The level case","A fridge leaning back does half the closing for you.","The hinge check","Sagging doors misalign the seal's contact line.","The cost of leaks","Frost, energy waste and the compressor's extra hours.","When to replace","Hairline gasket cracks versus the whole part.","The fridge seal is a three-cause problem with a ten-cent test. Run the test first and the fix is usually the cheapest one on the list.","writers"],
["writers/learn/types-of-writing/how-to-write-a-blog-post","The Blog Post Skeleton","A blog post works as a service document: promise in the headline, answer early, proof in the middle and one clear takeaway at the end. The skeleton is fixed and the voice fills it.","The promise headline","Say what the reader gets, in the reader's own words.","Answer early","The conclusion first: blogs are read backwards often.","The proof middle","Examples, steps and data in the order they help.","The takeaway","One thing the reader does differently tomorrow.","Subhead discipline","Skimmers are the actual audience; subheads serve them.","The voice layer","Personality is the difference between posts that spread.","The blog post is service writing with a personality budget. Keep the skeleton honest and the posts keep getting found.","writers"],
["writers/learn/writing-basics","The Foundations Index","Writing basics is the order of the ladder: sentences and paragraphs, then structure and voice, then the shapes of the main forms. This index links the whole floor, and the sequence is the point.","Sentences first","The basic units, learned before anything fancy.","Paragraph logic","One idea per paragraph: the oldest useful rule.","Structure","The map that keeps readers oriented through long pieces.","Voice","The part that sounds like you, taught after the mechanics.","Forms","The main shapes: memo, essay, pitch, report.","Practice","The drills that make the basics automatic.","The basics are called basics because everything else stands on them. Follow the ladder in order and the fancy skills arrive on schedule.","writers"],
["writers/tested","What Tested Means","BRYME Tested marks opportunities the desk has personally used: submitted, accepted, published or paid, each with dates and the account kept separate from research. The standard is firsthand or nothing, and the label means exactly that.","The standard","Firsthand experience or the label does not apply.","What gets tested","Submissions, payments and the actual response behaviour.","The dates","Every test carries the window it happened in.","Kept separate","Tested records never blend into researched listings.","What failures teach","Rejections and unresponsiveness are also recorded.","How to read the badge","The badge is a claim with a date attached.","Tested is a promise of firsthand evidence: the desk did the thing and dated the doing. The badge carries its proof with it.","money"],
["entertainment/best-thriller-movies-of-all-time","The Canon Of Tension","The thriller canon runs on control of information: what the audience knows, when they know it and what the protagonist can see. The ten here are chosen for construction rather than shock, and the tension taxonomy explains why each works.","Construction over shock","The films that hold without cheap tricks.","The information games","Suspense, surprise and dramatic irony as three tools.","The wrong-man shape","Innocence hunted: the genre's most durable engine.","The heist layer","Thrills built from procedure and clock.","The psychological tier","Where the threat lives between the ears.","Where to start","Three entries for three different tolerances.","A thriller is an information machine. Watch these ten with the taxonomy in mind and the craft becomes as enjoyable as the ride.","home"],
["home/running-toilet-cistern-fix","The Three Culprits","A toilet that never stops running has three usual culprits: the flapper, the fill valve and the float height. Each has a symptom, each costs under a part-price dinner, and the whole repair is the gateway to household plumbing.","The flapper first","The rubber that degrades and the chain that tangles.","The fill valve","Hissing and slow fills point past the flapper.","The float height","Water level settings that cause constant trickle.","The dye test","Food colouring in the tank settles the diagnosis in minutes.","Part prices","The three parts and their honest shelf lives.","When it is the valve","Fill valves are cheap; replacement beats repair.","The running cistern is plumbing's cheapest victory: three culprits, three parts and a repair that teaches the whole flush system.","tech"],
["tech/bluetooth-not-pairing","The Ritual, In Order","Pairing failures are stale records and wrong modes: clear the old pairing on both ends, put the device in the right discover mode and re-pair clean. The ritual's order matters and the diagnostic tells are named.","Connected elsewhere","The most common cause is the least suspected.","The stale record","Old pairing data corrupts new attempts routinely.","The clean ritual","Forget, reset, re-pair: the order that works.","Discover modes","Pairing mode is not always discoverable mode.","The name game","Device names hide behind model numbers.","Two-reset rule","After two clean failures, believe the hardware.","Bluetooth pairing is a handshake with stale memory. Run the ritual in order and the device remembers how to talk again.","writers"],
["writers/learn/professional-writing/how-to-write-a-work-report","The Report Skeleton","A work report serves a decision: summary first, evidence second, recommendation last, and every figure dated and sourced. The skeleton is the same for interns and directors and the length discipline is part of the craft.","Summary first","The busy reader's version lives at the top.","The evidence","Dated figures with their sources named beside them.","Recommendation","What should happen, who owns it and by when.","The audience test","The same facts, re-cut for the actual reader.","Length discipline","One page forces the right editorial choices.","The appendix instinct","Detail belongs behind the decision, not inside it.","Work reports are decision tools wearing document form. Keep the skeleton and the reports get read in the meeting they were written for.","writers"],
["writers/writing-opportunities","How The Opportunity Map Works","The opportunity map indexes every BRYME listing by country and genre: each row carries its pay status, rights note and the date it was verified, and the map's coverage claims are stated honestly alongside the gaps.","By country and genre","The two axes that make the map browsable.","Pay statuses","Confirmed, reported and unconfirmed: three honest labels.","Rights notes","What each listing actually sells, in plain words.","Verified dates","The date each row's source was last checked.","The coverage claims","What the desk has checked versus what exists.","How to use it","A weekly routine for working the map rather than browsing it.","The opportunity map is a research instrument: dated rows, labelled pay and honest gaps. Work it on a schedule and it behaves like a pipeline.","home"],
["home/is-it-cheaper-to-heat-one-room","The Honest Thermodynamics","Heating one room is cheaper only when the house's heat loss and the boiler's behaviour cooperate: the honest answer runs fabric heat loss, radiator balance and the condensing-boiler curve. The rule of thumb and its exceptions are both stated.","The thermodynamics","Heat moves to cold; closed rooms leak to cold ones.","The condensing curve","Why low flow temperatures save the real money.","Radiator balancing","The adjustment that changes room-to-room costs.","The rule of thumb","When one-room heating genuinely wins.","The exceptions","Poor insulation flips the answer for whole floors.","Thermostat habits","Scheduled heat beats manual toggling almost always.","The one-room heating question has a physics answer and a house-specific answer. Read the thermodynamics and then read your own radiators.","writers"],
["writers/guides/how-long-should-you-wait-for-an-editor","The Waiting Windows","Waiting for an editor has published norms: the guidelines' window plus one week, two follow-ups maximum and a calendar that decides when silence becomes an answer. The windows are recorded honestly and the anxiety math is laid out.","The guidelines window","The publication's stated timeline is the only official clock.","Plus one week","The grace period every professional allows.","Two follow-ups","The maximum before silence becomes information.","The anxiety math","Why waiting feels longer than it is, and what helps.","The simultaneous question","Pitching elsewhere during the window, honestly handled.","When silence is the answer","The move-on list and its dignity.","Waiting is part of the submission process with its own norms. Keep the calendar honest and the waiting stops running your week.","home"],
["home/roof-gutter-leak-joint","The Joint, The Slope, The Hanger","Gutter leaks come from joints, slope or hangers: the joint reseals in an afternoon, the slope adjusts with a level and the hangers re-seat under the roofline. The repair ladder runs all three in cost order.","The joint","Where sections meet is where water leaves.","The slope","Gutters fall toward downspouts; levels settle the argument.","The hanger","Sagging runs re-seat with fasteners and patience.","The sealant question","Which sealants survive freeze-thaw cycles.","The debris cause","Blocked runs overflow at joints and read as leaks.","When to replace","Fascia damage flips the repair-replace maths.","Gutter leaks are a three-cause problem with a ladder of cheap fixes. Diagnose by the leak's position and the repair stays on schedule.","sports"],
