["home/spring-home-reset","The Order That Works","The spring reset works in one order: air first (filters and vents), then water (fixtures and hoses), then heat (shutdowns and servicing), then the outside. The order saves repeat trips and the checklist dates itself.","Air first","Filters, vents and the dryer duct's annual visit.","Water second","Hoses, shutoffs and the outdoor taps' reawakening.","Heat third","Boiler and furnace shutdowns before summer storage.","Outside last","Gutters, roofline and the garden's infrastructure.","The dated list","Everything above in a printable sequence.","The budget view","Which resets save money and which simply prevent loss.","The spring reset is an order-of-operations problem. Follow the sequence once and the house survives the hot months without surprises.","sports"],
